* ============================================================================
* workspace_minidb.dts -- a whole database inside one memo field (AIF-070's
* chartered destination, LANDED 2026-08-11 on owner's "do it"). WORKSPACE
* SAVE <name> MEMO MINIDB writes a MINIDB 1 container: the self-locating v3
* posture PLUS every open table's bytes and every attached native index's
* bytes, length-prefixed (binary-safe -- the memo store is payload-agnostic,
* runtime-proven by the zoo on embedded NULs). WORKSPACE LOAD <name> MEMO RAM
* detects the container and hydrates FROM THE PAYLOAD: table bytes flow
* memo -> RAM VFS with ZERO disk reads, then the carried posture stands the
* areas up re-pointed at RAM. Reads are residence-aware (a RAM-resident
* source is read from ramfs), so a RAM session can save its working set
* whole. Plain WORKSPACE LOAD <name> MEMO refuses a MINIDB payload with the
* hydration instruction rather than half-loading.
*
* RUNTIME-PROVEN 2026-08-11 (build 18:35:35, FIRST TRY): mcc_db saved at
* 94200 B (92139 B of table+index bytes + 1443 B posture), oracle
* byte-compare OK on the whole container; hydrated onto a CLEAN RAM disk in
* 65.5 ms -- faster than the disk-sourced hydration (71-94 ms), memory to
* memory; STUDENTS read (200 recs), ENROLL's CDX attached from memo-carried
* bytes via the native fallback; unmount dropped everything, leaving the
* memo as the database's only running-copy source.
*
* Run: DO workspace_minidb | regression: REGRESSION RUN WORKSPACE_MINIDB
* Markers: DB_T1 (row readable from memo-carried table), DB_T2 (order
* attached from memo-carried index), DB_T3/DB_T4 (memo SIDECAR carriage,
* added 2026-08-12 -- AIF-108 [SIDECAR] unblock).
*
* Act 2 sidecar proof shape: the DTX layer bypasses the ramfs, so a
* RAM-session sidecar is really disk-resident under the mount dir and
* SURVIVES unmount as residue. A naive roundtrip check could therefore go
* green off the residue. So after saving the container, the script POISONS
* the live sidecar value; only then does it unmount, remount, and hydrate.
* DB_T3 green means the hydrated value came from the CONTAINER (hydration
* truncate-overwrites the residue), not from leftovers. DB_T4 proves the
* hydrated sidecar is writable. Residue note: MDMEMO.dtx remains on real
* disk under data\ram after the run (harmless; truncated by the next run).
* ============================================================================
SET ECHO OFF
STOP_ON_ERROR OFF

FORMULA "WS-MINIDB-PROOF-BEGIN"

* --- author the container from the disk-resident MCC ------------------------
* AMENDED 2026-08-28. 'WORKSPACE LOAD mcc_x64' read a posture FILE from the
* PRODUCTION workspaces directory, which the AIF-078 L2 bracket redirects away
* from. The posture is now built here.
*
* THE THREE AREAS THE ARMS READ ARE KEPT AT THEIR mcc_x64 SLOTS: DB_T1 reads
* SELECT 8 (STUDENTS, LNAME) and DB_T2 reads SELECT 4 (ENROLL, SET ORDER TAG
* SID). mcc_x64 held ENROLL at AREA 4 and STUDENTS at AREA 8, so opening them
* into the same slots keeps both markers and their meanings untouched. DEPT is
* opened at AREA 3, also its mcc_x64 slot, so the container is not degenerate.
* Three areas rather than thirteen; the count was never the claim -- carriage
* THROUGH the minidb container is.
DO x64
WORKSPACE CLOSE
SELECT 3
USE DEPT
SELECT 4
USE ENROLL
SELECT 8
USE STUDENTS
WORKSPACE SAVE minidb_regress MEMO MINIDB
WORKSPACE CLOSE

* --- clean RAM disk: the memo is the ONLY source ----------------------------
DO mem
WORKSPACE LOAD minidb_regress MEMO RAM

* --- the database came out of the memo --------------------------------------
VDISK STATUS
SELECT 8
TOP
? "DB_T1_students_from_memo:" + (LNAME > "")
SELECT 4
SET ORDER TAG SID
? "DB_T2_index_from_memo:" + (SID >= 1)

* --- act 2: memo sidecar carriage (AIF-108 [SIDECAR] unblock) ---------------
WORKSPACE CLOSE
SELECT 1
CREATE X64 MDMEMO (ID N(4,0), NOTES M)
APPEND
REPLACE ID WITH 1
REPLACE NOTES WITH "carried through the container"
WORKSPACE SAVE minidb_sidecar MEMO MINIDB

* poison the LIVE sidecar so residue and container disagree -- a green below
* can only come from container bytes
REPLACE NOTES WITH "residue, must not survive hydration"
CLOSE
VDISK UNMOUNT
DO mem
WORKSPACE LOAD minidb_sidecar MEMO RAM
* ADDRESSED BY NAME, NOT BY SLOT -- and this is the second time this file has
* had to learn it. The container was authored with the table in area 1, so the
* posture records AREA 1 and nothing at 0: a SPARSE posture. Under R130 a
* posture's AREA number is a KEY, not an engine address, so the load allocates
* the lowest free slot in the current workspace -- slot 0 -- and announces the
* remap. `SELECT 1` then reached an EMPTY area and DB_T3/DB_T4 both read .F.
* while the container bytes were perfectly fine (measured 2026-08-27: the arm
* was followed by "REPLACE: no file open", which is what an empty area says).
* MDMEMO is unique in this session, so the name is unambiguous here -- see
* AIF-140 for when it is not.
SELECT MDMEMO
? "DB_T3_memo_value_from_container:" + (NOTES = "carried through the container")
REPLACE NOTES WITH "post-hydration write"
? "DB_T4_sidecar_writable_after_hydration:" + (NOTES = "post-hydration write")

FORMULA "WS-MINIDB-PROOF-END"

* --- teardown ----------------------------------------------------------------
WORKSPACE CLOSE
VDISK UNMOUNT
DO x64
